## Repository Structure

```
.
├── Li_Mapping_with_SOM_PCA.ipynb   # Main analysis notebook (preprocessing → PCA → SOM → K-Means)
├── Datasets/
│   └── AST_L1T/                    # Raw ASTER L1T single-band GeoTIFFs (not tracked by git)
├── output/
│   ├── ASTER_datacube_reproj_clipped.tif   # Preprocessed 9-band datacube
│   ├── aster_kmeans_filtered.png           # K-Means result (majority-filtered)
│   ├── aster_som_map_raw.png               # SOM neuron map
│   └── aster_som_spectral_curves.png       # Dominant endmember spectra
└── README.md
```

---
## Roadmap

The following extensions are planned or in progress:

- [ ] **Stacked Autoencoder** dimensionality reduction (following Nagar et al. 2024) as a non-linear alternative to PCA
- [ ] Canonical Autoencoder baseline for comparison
- [ ] Multi-source fusion: integrate Sentinel-2 (10 m VNIR/SWIR) and Landsat 9 over the same AOI
- [ ] Cross-validation against available geological mapping of the Tete Province
- [ ] Spectral angle mapper (SAM) comparison against USGS/ASTER mineral libraries
- [ ] Export cluster polygons to GeoJSON for overlay with structural geology data

---

## Reference

This project directly adapts the framework from:

> Nagar, S., Farahbakhsh, E., Awange, J., & Chandra, R. (2024). *Remote sensing framework for geological mapping via stacked autoencoders and clustering.* Advances in Space Research. [arXiv:2404.02180](https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.02180)

